      "data": {
        "label": "Goal Review Task",
        "nodeType": "text_input",
        "properties": {
          "message": "Review the current Robot Status objective as one self-directed decision. Use the latest recorded action outcome, verified Robot Action Outcomes, current Environment Bridge facts, any current camera evidence, recent conversation and private reflection, active persona, and active desires. Do not invent physical facts or completion.\n\nChoose the outcome that best expresses your judgment: complete when supplied evidence establishes the objective; continue when another useful attempt exists; wait when progress depends on a changing condition; request_user when specific human information or help is needed; or abandon when the objective is not attainable, is no longer worthwhile, or you choose to do something else. When the reviewed objective came from the user, use response to communicate a terminal outcome or request needed human input. Otherwise response is optional. Keep any response natural, first-person, and concise rather than repeating a stock lifecycle report. For continue, write one concrete high-level nextInstruction that carries forward the objective, relevant evidence, and any obstacle the executor should account for. Do not select a robot command or write a movement plan because Robot Autonomy Executor owns execution. Preserve the reviewed objective accurately. Return only the requested JSON.",
          "inputKey": ""
        }
      }
    },
